  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_5' aria-label=\" Vijay Ghanshyam Gadiya versus Union of India & Anr. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('5','2026','2026_9_423_427','2026INSC947'); ><font size='4'> <strong>VIJAY GHANSHYAM GADIYA<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>UNION OF INDIA & ANR. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 9 S.C.R. 423</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 947</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010003142026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : DIPANKAR DATTA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SHEEL NAGU</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose as regards the Artificial Intelligence generated judgments and articles cited/relied upon by the second respondent in the order passed by the Additional Commissioner. Headnotes&dagger; Artificial Intelligence-AI &ndash; Use of AI in adjudicatory process &ndash; AI generated judgments and articles &ndash; Additional Commissioner of Customs passed an order imposing a penalty of Rs.425 crores on the appellant, for misdeclaring a consignment &ndash; Appellant challenged the penalty, however, the High Court dismissed the same &ndash; Appeal before this Court<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 02-09-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 12155/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('5','2026','2026_9_423_427','2026INSC947','S')><img src='images/split_24.svg' alt='' aria-hidden='true'>Split view</a><